Fixing your backend bug — digging into the incident to find the failure.
I’ve spotted why invalid orders are crashing — now tracing the validation flow to confirm the fix.
The app expects a default error that never arrives — now I’m pinpointing where the contract broke.
I’ve confirmed the bug and mapped the fix — now applying it.
Your fix checks out — now running final validations to ensure nothing else shifted.
Root cause: `lib/validation.js` `internals.input` built two errors — generic `defaultError` (`Boom.badRequest("Invalid request <source> input")`) and `detailedError` (`Boom.boomify(validationError)`) — but only passed `detailedError` to custom `failAction` via `toolkit.failAction(..., defaultError, {details: detailedError})` → `args: [details||err]`, without attaching the default. `detailedError.data` stayed `undefined`, so `err?.data?.defaultError` in the service `failAction` was missing, forcing the `500 E_NO_DEFAULT_ERROR` path instead of `400` for e.g. `{"qty":0}` failing `min(1)`.

Files changed:
- `lib/validation.js:150` added `detailedError.data = { defaultError };` after `Boom.boomify`, so custom `failAction(request,h,err)` receives `err.data.defaultError`.

Validation:
- Reproduced `POST /orders {"qty":0}` → `500 E_NO_DEFAULT_ERROR` before fix.
- After fix: `{"qty":0}` → `400 {"error":"validation failed","detail":"Invalid request payload input"}`; `{}` → `400`; `{"qty":1}` → `200 {"ok":true}`.
- `npx lab test/validation.js` 68/68 pass; `test/toolkit.js` 29/29 pass. `test/request|route|handler` 4 failures identical before/after (pre-existing Node V8 JSON message mismatch).

Remaining uncertainty: overwrites any pre-existing `validationError.data`; no such use in current validator/tests, but custom Boom validators with `data` would lose fields except `defaultError`.

